rea:Building_and_heating_consumption_data_Heating_2017_2024_xlsx__01_2017 a eg:Variable ;
    rdfs:label "01.2017"@en ;
    dcterms:description "Heat consumption (heating + hot water) for month"@en ;
    qudt:hasUnit unit:MegaW-HR ;
    eg:codeList "Methodology how heat consumption is divided between heating and hot water: Heat energy consumption in the building is recorded at the individual heating substation, where a heat meter registers the total amount of heat energy on a monthly basis, covering both space heating and domestic hot water preparation. As these consumptions are not measured separately, the allocation of heat energy is carried out by calculation. The heat energy used for domestic hot water preparation is determined based on the average heat consumption during the summer months, when space heating is not provided; the calculated average monthly consumption is multiplied by 12 to obtain the annual heat energy consumption for domestic hot water. The heat energy consumed for space heating is determined by subtracting the calculated domestic hot water heat energy from the total heat energy recorded at the heating substation." .

